course: dictionary
lesson: 9606
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word «string» has many meanings. A string can be a thin cord for tying things, a tight wire on a guitar, or a row of things on a thread. The words around it show you which meaning is right. That is context, and it is your best clue.
explain: «Let go of a ball swung on a string and it flies off in a straight line, not in a curve.» The ball is on a cord, so string means a thin cord here. Swap in your meaning: "a ball swung on a thin cord" still makes sense, so you have chosen well.
explain: «Short, thin, tight strings wobble fast and sound high» is about music. The words wobble, sound high and tight tell you that a string here is a wire on an instrument. The word stayed the same, but the clues changed its meaning.
explain: Sometimes string is a verb. «To string» means to put things on a thread, as in stringing beads. When you meet string, ask which meaning fits the sentence.
fact: A string is a thin cord used for tying things, like a ball of string.
fact: On a guitar, violin or piano, a string is a tight wire or thread that makes a sound when it moves.
fact: A string of things is a row of them on a thread, like a string of beads, or a series, like a string of wins.
fact: To string means to put things on a thread.
fact: «No strings attached» means with no hidden conditions.
exercise: «Let go of a ball swung on a string and it flies off in a straight line.» What is a string here? | A row of beads | A series of wins | A wire on a guitar | *A thin cord for tying things
exercise: «The sitar has sympathetic strings that nobody plucks.» What are the strings in this sentence? | A ball of string | A cord for tying parcels | *Tight wires that make sounds | A row of letters in a computer
exercise: Maya says, «She has a string of wins this season.» What does string mean? | *A series, one win after another | A tight wire on a guitar | To put beads on a thread | A piece of cord for tying
test: «He will help you, with no strings attached.» What does this mean? | It is tied up with cord | *It has no hidden conditions | It is tight and high like a wire | It is a row of beads on a thread
test: What does string mean in «Mia began to string the beads for her necklace»? | A thin cord for tying | A series of wins | *To put things on a thread | A tight wire that makes a sound
exam: What does string mean in «Short, thin, tight strings wobble fast and sound high»? | A thin cord for tying parcels | *A tight wire that makes a sound when it wobbles | A series of wins | A row of beads on a thread
